  "body": "Closes #1181\nClaim: cloud/m4q-small-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/m4q-small-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/r1181-opus-r2)\n\n**Problem.** The four Réglages ⓘ rows (« Bouton + », navigateur par défaut, synchro iCloud, citations minimum) open a popover forced on iPhone (`presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)`) around text with `fixedSize` and no `ScrollView`: at large text sizes the explanation can be clipped (HIG › Popovers: no popovers in compact views).\n\n**Cause.** `InfoBubbleButton` forces the popover on compact width and the content cannot scroll.\n\n**Change.** `InfoBubbleButton` no longer forces the adaptation: the system picks the form (popover on wide views, sheet in a compact one) and the content fits both, without guessing which: `ViewThatFits(in: .vertical)` shows the bubble as is when it fits, else inside a `ScrollView` (leading-aligned); sheet detents `[.medium, .large]` and a drag indicator are always set (a popover ignores them). The four call sites and all strings are untouched (#1334 « tu » has no file in common; #571's PR neither). **Decision to confirm before merge:** this is option 1 of the issue and departs on iPhone from the « bubble » of the operator decision of 2026-11-17 (#1062, #1065); the issue states it is (b); the other options (ScrollView inside a forced popover, section footer) need a size measured on a simulator.\n\n**Tests.** `InfoBubblePresentationTests` pins the detents only (it fails without the change because `InfoBubblePresentation` does not exist). That the content is reachable in whichever form the system picks cannot be shown by a unit test here: the Mac check below is the real check. Cloud session: not built here (no Xcode), compile-check requested.\n\n**Mac check owed on #893** (`host: mac-helps`), stated neutrally: whatever form the system picks (iPhone portrait, a Plus/Pro Max in landscape, iPad), at the largest accessibility text size, the « Bouton + » and iCloud-sync bubbles show their whole text (scrolling if needed). Also judge: a short bubble in a `.medium` sheet is centred rather than top-left (Opus round 2, finding 1); dragging between `.medium` and `.large` must not reset the scroll position (finding 2). If either shows, the alternatives are a leading/top frame on the `ViewThatFits`, or always a `ScrollView { bubble() }.scrollBounceBehavior(.basedOnSize)`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEncUK39uqEYPwrtn4)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEncUK39uqEYPwrtn4",
